==Battleground==
*3 [[Haniwanwan]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*3 [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*3 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Loris]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Primeval Cyclone]] spawns as the boss after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Haniwanwan]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Any [[:Category:anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] Crowd Controllers such as [[Talents|Talented]] [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Rodeo Cat]] or [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Mystic Uril]] are heavily recommanded to slow down the Primeval Cyclone. [[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]] and true form of [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]] in particular can trivialise this stage.
Pair them with high Anti-Relic DPS such as [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:N2]] and you can easily beat this stage.

If you have [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]], you can use them instead of other Anti-Relic Crowd Control to weaken Primeval Cyclone, but you need to lure them near the base due of its slow speed.

